# docs/loop/goal.criteria — the terminus for the loop. HUMAN-OWNED.
#
# The loop runs until EVERY active criterion passes. Nothing else counts as done:
# not the agent's report, not a tidy diff, not a green doc.
#
# Format, one criterion per line, pipe-separated:
#
#   id | title | shell command | expected exit | expected output substring (optional) | timeout seconds
#
# ID convention (the verifier reads it):
#   F*  floor   — regression gates that must always be green (the repo's own gates)
#   T*  target  — the work in flight. The goal is "met" only when a target exists
#                 AND every active criterion passes. No target => GOAL: UNDEFINED.
#
# Rules for writing these:
#   - No pipe characters, including `||` (they are the field separator). Use
#     `if ...; then exit 0; fi; ...`. The verifier rejects malformed rows loudly.
#   - Behaviour, not implementation: assert on responses, exit codes and grep-able
#     output, never on "file X exists".
#   - Affordable, because every iteration re-runs the whole file: keep the floor
#     under ~60s total. Heavy gates (preflight_selftest, Compose E2E) are listed in
#     docs/loop/GOAL.md as deep checks, not here.
#   - Change the product docs first, then this file. Never edit either to make a
#     failing iteration pass.

# --- floor: the repo's real gates, as already documented in TESTING.md ---------
F1 | Redis test DB 15 is reachable | redis-cli -p 6399 ping | 0 | PONG | 15
F2 | backend suite passes in the ots-dev image | docker run --rm --network=host -v "$PWD":/app -v ots-bundle:/bundle -e BUNDLE_PATH=/bundle -w /app ots-dev bundle exec rspec | 0 | 0 failures | 900
F3 | frontend unit tests pass | npm --prefix frontend test --silent | 0 | | 300
F4 | frontend typecheck passes | npm --prefix frontend run typecheck | 0 | | 300
F5 | frontend production build passes | npm --prefix frontend run build | 0 | | 300

# --- target: uncomment to arm the loop --------------------------------------
# Nothing is armed right now, so scripts/loop_verify.sh reports GOAL: UNDEFINED
# and scripts/loop.sh refuses to start. That is deliberate: the floor is already
# green, so the loop has no honest work to do until a human names one.
#
# The only TODO in TASKS.md today is T-78 (landing route from the approved copy
# in replica/launch/landing.md). Uncomment the two lines below to arm it, and the
# loop will build the route, the view, and their tests until both pass.
#
#T1 | /landing serves the approved landing page | docker run --rm --network=host -v "$PWD":/app -v ots-bundle:/bundle -e BUNDLE_PATH=/bundle -w /app ots-dev bundle exec rspec spec/integration/landing_spec.rb | 0 | 0 failures | 900
#T2 | landing view renders the approved headline | npm --prefix frontend test --silent -- landing | 0 | | 300
#
# For any other target, take the TASKS.md / KNOWN_ISSUES.md ID you are closing and
# write one criterion per observable behaviour it promises. One criterion that
# cannot be satisfied by editing a mock is worth five that can.
